<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Robert Semple</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1777–1816</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Robert Semple was an American-born merchant and travel writer who became governor-in-chief of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hudsons-bay-company">Hudson's Bay Company</a>'s territories in 1815. Sent to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-river-colony">Red River Colony</a> amid its conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-company">North West Company</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metis">Métis</a>, he was killed together with about twenty of his men at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-seven-oaks">Battle of Seven Oaks</a> on 19 June 1816.</p></div>
